From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:19:47 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Windows 10 Mobile: Chrome's views on the engine's one aura
 root

The phone gives an app one window (the shell's panel) and the engine one
aura root in it, with no HWND. Chrome's widgets become NativeWidgetAura
windows under that root, as on ChromeOS:
- ChromeViewsDelegate::CreateNativeWidget and CreateNativeWidget always
  make a NativeWidgetAura, with the root as context when none is given;
  a DesktopNativeWidgetAura that slips through is fatal at once, naming
  the widget, rather than a second compositor nobody shows.
- The maximized browser window draws no title bar or caption buttons
  (WindowManagerProvidesTitleBar); dialogs keep theirs.
- No status tray (StatusTrayWin CHECKs a window class it cannot register).
- Tabs are not dragged out into windows of their own.
- The main browser window's minimum width is 320 DIP, not 500: a phone
  held upright is 360 to 412 wide.
- No Win32 system menu on a long press beside the tabs, and no Move,
  Size, Minimize, Maximize or Restore items in the views system menu.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
